<title>BELGIUM: EU still to notify France on gene-maize.</title>
<headline>EU still to notify France on gene-maize.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>France has not yet been officially notified of a decision to allow the import of genetically modified maize into the European Union, a European Commission spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>The spokesman was commenting on a European Commission decision of December 18 to clear imports of maize developed by Swiss firm Ciba Geigy AG and grown in the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;It's imminent,&quot; Environment spokesman Peter Joergensen told a news briefing, repeating a statement he made on January 9.</p>
<p>Joergensen gave no reason for the delay.</p>
<p>France has said it will not approve imports of modified maize until the introduction of new EU labelling rules which would take some time, the Commission has said.</p>
<p>Washington warned earlier this month that undue delay by France in implementing the EU decision could lead to a new transatlantic trade dispute.</p>
</text>
